   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1948-01-09">Jan. 9, 1948.</date><lb/>
             <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs>,<lb/>
            <rs ref="#" type="place">East Hampton, Long Island, N.Y.</rs></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Mr.
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>Some of the former students of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4764" type="person">Dr.
            Leo Baeck</rs>, have felt that his visit to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__105"
            type="place">Chicago</rs> would be an appropriate time for academic honors, if
            former German scholars, like yourself, felt that his academic achievements entitled
            him to such honors.</p>
            <p>I discussed the matter with <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4765" type="person"
                  >President Ernest Colwell</rs> of the University of <rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__105" type="place">Chicago</rs>, and out of the suggestion
               came a plan that I write to yourself and some of the other men, who we thought knew
                  <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4764" type="person">Dr. Baeck</rs> and his work.</p>
            <p>You will recall that while you were still at home <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4764"
                  type="person">Dr. Baeck</rs> was teaching at the Hochschule in <rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__37" type="place">Berlin</rs>. Of course when the plague
               came into <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>, he, like
               others, was put in the concentration camp, from which he was fortunately rescued by
               the American army.</p>
            <p><add place="below" hand="#tillich_person_id__1928"><hi rend="hand">
                     <!-- author vermutlich Tillich? --><hi rend="underline">I am not</hi> but <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1209" type="person">Adolph</rs> may know somebody
                     in New School who is! please write a letter <unclear>in this sense</unclear>
                     you have found somebody! <rs rend="#tillich_person_id__4766" type="person"
                        >Leo.Strauss</rs> Ki3-0186 re <unclear>to</unclear></hi></add>I know that
               you are <hi rend="underline">well acquainted</hi> with <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__4764" type="person">Baeck</rs> and his work. If you feel
               that he is worthy of an honory degree from the University, I would ask you to write a
               letter to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4765" type="person">Dr. Ernest Colwell</rs> to
               that effect. The matter rests altogether with you.</p>
            <p>You will, of course, have no idea who I am, although when you were at the University of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__105" type="place">Chicago</rs>
            I learned to know you, unfortunately, only casually. I hope you will be able to agree with us in this matter.</p>
            <p>Thanking you for anything you might feel you want to do, I remain</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Cordially yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__608" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">George Fox</hi></rs></signed><lb/>
               GGF:L
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
